.TH CHTTP_TLS_DEFAULT 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Macros"
.SH NAME
CHTTP_TLS_DEFAULT \- default TLS configuration initialiser
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <chttp.h>

CHTTP_TLS_DEFAULT
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Expands to a chttp_tls_config_t initialiser with:
  verify_peer    = true
  verify_host    = true
  ca_bundle_path = NULL  (use system CA bundle)
  cert_path      = NULL  (no client certificate)
  key_path       = NULL  (no client key)
.fi
.PP
verify_host always implies verify_peer in practice: hostname matching
against a certificate whose chain was never validated gives no real
security guarantee, since the certificate itself could be forged.
Setting verify_peer = false with verify_host left at true (the
CHTTP_TLS_DEFAULT value) still performs full certificate verification.
To disable all server certificate checking, set both verify_peer and
verify_host to false.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
chttp_tls_config_t tls = CHTTP_TLS_DEFAULT;
tls.verify_peer = false;
tls.verify_host = false;
chttpclient_set_tls(cli, &tls);
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR chttpclient_set_tls (3)
